{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>And Lot's two daughters conceived.</b> Rashi: they controlled themselves and brought forth their testimony. This is the reading in the Paris manuscript, which lacks the word עדות; and a proof is from Bereshit Rabbati, ״ואלה בתולי בתי״ — עדות בתי (i.e., the בתי form functions as עדות). And we do not read ערותן with a resh. Furthermore, for in the practice of that place, עדות refers to their virginity, and they would engage in harlotry elsewhere, and they were so tightly closed up below that they expelled the virginity, which is their עדות."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The text appears to offer a regional-linguistic explanation for the unusual term; the last clause is obscure and translated hyper-literally. The referent of ה״‎ג (הגירסא, 'the reading') and the exact syntax of the Bereshit Rabbati citation are uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:00.620695627Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}